# THE SEPARATE BUILD, with cross-boundary early cutoff: what `term make` runs (`--merged` is the whole-program build).
# See note/project/term/compiler/incremental-compilation.md.
#
# The module graph the entry reaches splits into UNITS (its strongly connected components, compile/unit-graph.tree),
# and each unit is checked and emitted apart, in dependency order:
#   - a unit is checked against the STUBS of the units it reaches (their checked, body-less surface, compile/stubbing.tree),
#     never against their bodies
#   - a unit emits only its OWN modules, with imports reconnecting cross-unit references under the names each exports
#   - a unit's answer is cached keyed by its own content and what it reaches of its dependencies' surfaces, so an edit
#     that leaves a surface where it was replays every dependent unit from the cache: EARLY CUTOFF
#   - a unit is named the same way whichever entry reached it, so its module is one module
# It agrees with the merged build on what each file builds and refuses (`pnpm term:separate-diff`).
#
# Ported from compile/separate.ts `compileSeparate` and `portableBy` (item 0113 of term/self-host/change/001), which
# stays as the face. The decisions:
#   - `portableBy`'s two closures are the form `portable`, the roots they captured, run by `portable-write` and
#     `portable-read` (spec.md 4.9). A pass that takes the writing as a task (a stub's fingerprint, compile/stubbing.tree)
#     takes the pair the face makes of the form, `portable-tasks`
#   - the cache's two lookups take a build the cache runs on a miss. Term holds no closure, so that build is a
#     `unit-job` (the run, the unit, how it is checked), run by `job-stored` and `job-named-key`, which the face's
#     closure calls (spec.md 4.9)
#   - what the run cannot hold as Term (the import walk, the mill cache, compileProgram, the parse memo, the options'
#     lookups, a field's presence, the stored entry's JSON with its bigint tag) comes in `separate-given`, filled by the
#     face. A unit's answer is held as Term (`unit-answer`), and the face writes and reads the stored entry in the
#     original's shape, key for key, so an entry on disk is the bytes the original wrote (spec.md 4.15)
#   - docked: compile/cache (the text hash and the field hash, one memo for the process), compile/stub (the facts each
#     task carries, which hands the TypeScript analyses) and check/twin (the twin refusals)
#   - a route's calls and a dock statement are copied as the original spread them (`shallow-*`), so a renamed call is
#     written on a copy and the checked program keeps its own names

load @term/base/list
  find list
  find get
  find sort
  find join

load @term/base/hash
  find hash
  find get-or-default

load @term/base/maybe
  find maybe

load @term/base/text
  find split
  find char-at
  find last-index-of
  find substring
  find contains

load @term/base/ordering
  find from-texts
  find from-numbers

load ../parser/diagnostic
  find diagnostic

load ../parser/token
  find token-source

load ../parser/tree
  find parse-result
  find node

load ../parser/words
  find head-word

load ./node
  find statement
  find statement-span
  find twin
  find dock-route
  find dock-call
  find dock-method
  find dock-hook

load ./names
  find name-def
  find def-at
  find names-reached-indexed
  find names-printed

load ./stubbing
  find stub-known
  find stub-program
  find surface-hash
  find name-defs
  find names-used

load ./unit-graph
  find units
  find deck-root
  find portable-roots
  find portable-out
  find portable-in

load ./unit-mill
  find graph-template-set
  find graph-templates
  find entry-warnings

load ./explain
  find unit-inputs
  find why

dock load
  load <@term/make/code/compile/cache>, name separate-cache
  load <@term/make/code/compile/stub>, name separate-stub
  load <@term/make/code/check/twin>, name separate-twin

# ---- the deck roots as tokens ----

# A DECK'S ROOT WRITTEN AS A TOKEN, and read back as this machine's: the roots `portableBy`'s closures captured
form portable
  link roots, like list, like deck-root

# the two directions as tasks, for a pass that takes the writing as one. The face makes them of a `portable`
form portable-tasks
  link outward
    like task
      take given, like text
      like text
  link inward
    like task
      take given, like text
      like text

task portable-by
  take decks, like list, like deck-root
  like portable

  back
    make portable
      bind roots, portable-roots(decks)

task portable-write
  take held, like portable
  take given, like text
  like text

  back portable-out(held/roots, given)

task portable-read
  take held, like portable
  take given, like text
  like text

  back portable-in(held/roots, given)

# ---- what the build is handed ----

# one module's import scope as the import walk made it (compile/load.ts `ImportScope`): read here only for its finds,
# and handed on whole
form separate-scope
  link finds
    like hash
      like text
      like list, like text

# what the import walk answers (compile/load.ts `collectModules`)
form separate-collected
  link sources, like list, like token-source
  link diagnostics, like list, like diagnostic
  link scope
    like hash
      like text
      like separate-scope
  link edges
    like hash
      like text
      like list, like text

# one module milled, as compile.ts's `milledModule` answers it
form separate-milled
  link ok, like boolean
  link program
    like list, like statement
    need false
  link twins
    like list, like twin
    need false
  link diagnostics
    like list, like diagnostic
    need false

# one unit compiled (compile.ts `compileProgram`), as the face reads the result: every field there either way, the
# emitted modules as their files and emits in the result's order, and the roll and the obligations only when given
form separate-compiled
  link ok, like boolean
  link diagnostics, like list, like diagnostic
  link program, like list, like statement
  link modules, like list, like unit-file
  link warnings, like list, like diagnostic
  link roll, like maybe, like dynamic
  link open-claims, like list, like text
  link obligations, like maybe, like dynamic

# one emitted module of a unit
form unit-file
  link file, like text
  link emit, like dynamic

# one file's stubs
form unit-stubs
  link file, like text
  link statements, like list, like statement

# ONE UNIT'S BUILD: its own modules' emits, its public stub surface for dependents, its fingerprint, each stub
# definition as the name-level cutoff reads it, its routes and commands (`dock` statements, which no stub carries), the
# roll of its own definitions, and its warnings. A field a stored entry may lack is a maybe
form unit-build
  link files, like list, like unit-file
  link stubs, like list, like unit-stubs
  link interface-hash, like text
  link defs, like maybe, like list, like name-def
  link docks, like maybe, like list, like statement
  link roll, like maybe, like dynamic
  link warnings, like list, like diagnostic
  link open-claims, like maybe, like list, like text
  link obligations, like maybe, like dynamic

# a unit's answer: its build, or what refused it
form unit-answer
  link refused, like maybe, like list, like diagnostic
  link build, like maybe, like unit-build

# a definition the closure exports, the last of its name in dependency order: what an entry's shim re-exports
form export-entry
  link name, like text
  link exported, like text
  link file, like text
  link type, like boolean

# a unit's roll, by the unit's label
form unit-roll
  link label, like text
  link roll, like dynamic

# WHAT THE RUN CANNOT HOLD AS TERM READS IT, filled by the face
form separate-given
  # the import walk over the build's resolver, parse memo, scan cache and walk memo
  link collect
    like task
      like separate-collected
  # the options' lookups: the deck a file belongs to, its role (`<>` for none), its lean, and its module's name
  link deck-of
    like task
      take file, like text
      like maybe, like deck-root
  link role-of
    like task
      take file, like text
      like text
  link lean-of
    like task
      take file, like text
      like boolean
  link module-of
    like task
      take file, like text
      like text
  link parsed
    like task
      take unit, like token-source
      like parse-result
  # one module milled through the mill cache, with the graph's templates and their fingerprint
  link milled
    like task
      take unit, like token-source
      take templates, like hash, like text, like dynamic
      take template-key, like text
      like separate-milled
  # one unit's program compiled as `checked-as`, under `naming`, emitting only `files`
  link compile-unit
    like task
      take program, like list, like statement
      take checked-as, like text
      take scope
        like hash
          like text
          like separate-scope
      take naming, like text
      take files, like list, like text
      like separate-compiled
  # whether a statement carries a `stub-export`
  link has-stub-export
    like task
      take one, like statement
      like boolean
  link portable-tasks
    like task
      take held, like portable
      like portable-tasks
  # the checker's switches as a key (check/strict.ts `checkerSwitchKey`)
  link switch-key
    like task
      like text
  link env, like text
  # the build cache: whether there is one, the compiler's fingerprint for units, and its two lookups, each building
  # with the job on a miss
  link has-cache, like boolean
  link unit-version
    like task
      like text
  link cached-unit
    like task
      take key, like text
      take job, like unit-job
      like text
  link cached-name-key
    like task
      take key, like text
      take job, like unit-job
      like text
  # a unit's answer as the stored entry's JSON, and back: none when it does not read back as an answer
  link store
    like task
      take answer, like unit-answer
      like text
  link restore
    like task
      take stored, like text
      like maybe, like unit-answer
  # the run's answers, shared by a batch build's entries
  link has-units, like boolean
  link units
    like hash
      like text
      like unit-answer
  # `term make --explain`: the inputs a unit was last built from, and why each unit built this run was built
  link has-explain, like boolean
  link recall
    like task
      take id, like text
      like maybe, like unit-inputs
  link remember
    like task
      take id, like text
      take inputs, like unit-inputs
      like boolean
  link give-reasons
    like task
      take label, like text
      take reasons, like list, like text
      like boolean
  link keep-program, like boolean

# WHAT THE SEPARATE BUILD CAME TO: a refusal, or what the result is built from
form separate-answer
  link refused, like maybe, like list, like diagnostic
  link modules
    like hash
      like text
      like dynamic
  link warnings, like list, like diagnostic
  link open-claims, like maybe, like list, like text
  link obligations, like maybe, like dynamic
  link exports, like list, like export-entry
  link built, like list, like text
  link reused, like list, like text
  link closure-key, like text
  link natives, like list, like statement
  link docks, like list, like statement
  link rolls, like list, like unit-roll
  link program, like maybe, like list, like statement
  link surface, like list, like statement

# ONE BUILD'S RUN, made once and read by every unit
form separate-run
  mark shared
  link source, like token-source
  link given, like separate-given
  link portable, like portable
  link tasks, like portable-tasks
  link collected, like separate-collected
  link by-file
    like hash
      like text
      like token-source
  link order
    like list
      like list, like text
  # each unit's transitive dependency units
  link reach
    like list
      like hash
        like number
        like boolean
  # whether a proof above a unit runs its bodies
  link under-proof, like list, like boolean
  link template-set, like graph-template-set
  link builds, like list, like unit-build
  # each name to where it is defined, unit by unit, grown as units are answered (compile/names.tree)
  link name-index
    like hash
      like text
      like list, like def-at
  link unit-defs
    like list
      like list, like name-def
  # `keep-program`: the entry unit's checked program, when this run built it
  link entry-program, like maybe, like list, like statement

# ONE UNIT'S PART OF THE RUN, kept while it is answered
form unit-state
  mark shared
  link at, like number
  link files, like list, like text
  link label, like text
  link entry, like boolean
  link as-import, like text
  link as-self, like maybe, like text
  link dep-hashes, like list, like text
  link uses-templates, like boolean
  link used, like maybe, like list, like text
  link defs, like maybe, like list, like name-def
  # whether this run built the unit rather than replaying it
  link ran, like boolean
  # the `checked-as` the cache is being asked for, which a stored answer that cannot be read is built as
  link answering, like text

# the build a cache lookup runs on a miss: the unit, checked as `checked-as`
form unit-job
  link run, like separate-run
  link state, like unit-state
  link checked-as, like text

# ---- small helpers ----

task as-known
  take value, like dynamic
  like stub-known
  mark private

  back value

task as-diagnostics
  take value, like dynamic
  like list, like diagnostic
  mark private

  back value

# a shallow copy, as the original's spread. Natively a value is already a copy
bind shallow-statement
  take value, like statement
  like statement
  case node
    text <({...$value})>
  case browser
    text <({...$value})>
  case rust
    text <$value>
  case swift
    text <$value>
  case kotlin
    text <$value>

bind shallow-route
  take value, like dock-route
  like dock-route
  case node
    text <({...$value})>
  case browser
    text <({...$value})>
  case rust
    text <$value>
  case swift
    text <$value>
  case kotlin
    text <$value>

bind shallow-method
  take value, like dock-method
  like dock-method
  case node
    text <({...$value})>
  case browser
    text <({...$value})>
  case rust
    text <$value>
  case swift
    text <$value>
  case kotlin
    text <$value>

bind shallow-hook
  take value, like dock-hook
  like dock-hook
  case node
    text <({...$value})>
  case browser
    text <({...$value})>
  case rust
    text <$value>
  case swift
    text <$value>
  case kotlin
    text <$value>

bind shallow-call
  take value, like dock-call
  like dock-call
  case node
    text <({...$value})>
  case browser
    text <({...$value})>
  case rust
    text <$value>
  case swift
    text <$value>
  case kotlin
    text <$value>

# the stubs a unit is checked against, deep-copied, as the original's `structuredClone`: the checker annotates what it
# is handed, and one unit's stubs are read by every unit after it
bind copy-statements
  take value, like list, like statement
  like list, like statement
  case node
    text <structuredClone($value)>
  case browser
    text <structuredClone($value)>
  case rust
    text <$value>
  case swift
    text <$value>
  case kotlin
    text <$value>

task refused-answer
  take found, like list, like diagnostic
  like separate-answer
  mark private

  back
    make separate-answer
      bind refused, make(some, found)
      bind modules, make hash
      bind warnings, make list
      bind open-claims, make none
      bind obligations, make none
      bind exports, make list
      bind built, make list
      bind reused, make list
      bind closure-key, <>
      bind natives, make list
      bind docks, make list
      bind rolls, make list
      bind program, make none
      bind surface, make list

task job-of
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like unit-job
  mark private

  back
    make unit-job
      bind run, run
      bind state, state
      bind checked-as, checked-as

task refused-unit
  take found, like list, like diagnostic
  like unit-answer
  mark private

  back
    make unit-answer
      bind refused, make(some, found)
      bind build, make none

# the file a statement was written in, `<>` for none
task statement-file
  take one, like statement
  like text
  mark private

  save span-here, statement-span(one)
  sift span-here/file
    case some
      link known
      back known
    case none
      back <>

# a statement told the file it was written in
task filed-in
  take one, like statement
  take file-name, like text
  like statement
  mark private

  sift one
    case let
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case assign
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case expression
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case if
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case while
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case match
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case for-each
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case break
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case continue
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case return
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case exit
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case debug
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case probe
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case guard
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case throw
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case hold
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case function
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case record-type
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case mask
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case instance
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case native
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case bind
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case view
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case dock
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case roll
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
    case tell
      save one/span/file, make(some, file-name)
  back one

# a JavaScript word character, `\w`
task is-word-char
  take one, like text
  like boolean
  mark private

  fork test, not(is-equal(one/length, 1))
    hold
      back false
  back contains(<abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_>, one)

# whether a text writes the word `fuse` (`/\bfuse\b/`), cut once (one native pass) rather than searched from each place
task writes-fuse
  take given, like text
  like boolean
  mark private

  save pieces, split(given, <fuse>)
  save last-at, subtract(pieces/length, 1)
  save k, 0
  walk test
    hook test, is-below(k, last-at)
    hook hold
      save before, get(pieces, k)
      save after, get(pieces, add(k, 1))
      # the character before this `fuse`: its piece's last, or the `e` of the `fuse` before when the piece is empty
      save left-word, false
      fork test, is-above(before/length, 0)
        hold
          save left-word, is-word-char(char-at(before, subtract(before/length, 1)))
        miss
          save left-word, is-above(k, 0)
      # the character after: the next piece's first, or the `f` of the next `fuse` when that piece is empty
      save right-word, false
      fork test, is-above(after/length, 0)
        hold
          save right-word, is-word-char(char-at(after, 0))
        miss
          save right-word, is-below(add(k, 1), last-at)
      fork test, and(not(left-word), not(right-word))
        hold
          back true
      save k, add(k, 1)
  back false

# the name a split task was written with: `__in<g>_<k>` at its end removed
task written-of
  take name, like text
  like text
  mark private

  save at-in, last-index-of(name, <__in>)
  fork test, is-below(at-in, 0)
    hold
      back name
  save rest, substring(name, add(at-in, 4))
  save parts, split(rest, <_>)
  fork test, not(is-equal(parts/length, 2))
    hold
      back name
  walk parts
    take part
    fork test, is-equal(part/length, 0)
      hold
        back name
    walk split(part, <>)
      take digit
      fork test, not(and(is-equal(digit/length, 1), contains(<0123456789>, digit)))
        hold
          back name
  back substring(name, 0, at-in)

# ---- the routes ----

# A ROUTE NAMES ITS TASK AS THE TASK'S UNIT EXPORTS IT. The import binding binds a hook's `task bank` like a call, so
# where two files of the unit's program define the name the route carries `bank__in0_0`, a name of this unit's checked
# program only, and the run looked it up among the bundle's exports and failed (term-compiler-0064). Each call a route
# makes to another unit's task takes that task's exported name back
task exported-route-calls
  take docks, like list, like statement
  take program, like list, like statement
  take own, like hash, like text, like boolean
  take given, like separate-given
  like list, like statement
  mark private

  save has-export, given/has-stub-export
  save exported, make hash
  save renamed-count, 0
  walk program
    take one
    sift one
      case function
        link name
        link stub-export
        fork test, own/has(statement-file(one))
          hold
            turn next
        save written, written-of(name)
        fork test, not(is-equal(written, name))
          hold
            save renamed-count, add(renamed-count, 1)
            fork test, has-export(one)
              hold
                save exported/{name}, stub-export
              miss
                save exported/{name}, written
      miss
        turn next

  fork test, is-equal(renamed-count, 0)
    hold
      back docks

  save out, make list
  walk docks
    take one
    sift one
      case dock
        link route
        save statement-copy, shallow-statement(one)
        sift statement-copy
          case dock
            save statement-copy/route, route-renamed(route, exported)
          miss
            save nothing, 0
        push(out, statement-copy)
      miss
        push(out, one)
  back out

task call-renamed
  take one, like dock-call
  take exported, like hash, like text, like text
  like dock-call
  mark private

  fork test, exported/has(one/name)
    hold
      save call-copy, shallow-call(one)
      save call-copy/name, get-or-default(exported, one/name, one/name)
      back call-copy
  back one

task calls-renamed
  take calls, like list, like dock-call
  take exported, like hash, like text, like text
  like list, like dock-call
  mark private

  save out, make list
  walk calls
    take one
    push(out, call-renamed(one, exported))
  back out

task route-renamed
  take one, like dock-route
  take exported, like hash, like text, like text
  like dock-route
  mark private

  save route-copy, shallow-route(one)
  save route-copy/calls, calls-renamed(one/calls, exported)
  save methods-renamed, make list
  walk one/methods
    take method-one
    save method-copy, shallow-method(method-one)
    save method-copy/calls, calls-renamed(method-one/calls, exported)
    push(methods-renamed, method-copy)
  save route-copy/methods, methods-renamed
  save hooks-renamed, make list
  walk one/hooks
    take hook-one
    save hook-copy, shallow-hook(hook-one)
    save hook-copy/calls, calls-renamed(hook-one/calls, exported)
    push(hooks-renamed, hook-copy)
  save route-copy/hooks, hooks-renamed
  save children-renamed, make list
  walk one/children
    take child
    push(children-renamed, route-renamed(child, exported))
  save route-copy/children, children-renamed
  back route-copy

# ---- one unit's key ----

# the unit key's fields: its settings, then one per file. The first `settings-count` are its settings
task settings-count
  like number
  mark private

  back 6

# how a file is read, after its text's fingerprint: its role, its lean, its deck, and the name its module is imported by
task read-part
  take run, like separate-run
  take file, like text
  like text
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  save role-of, given/role-of
  save lean-of, given/lean-of
  save deck-of, given/deck-of
  save module-of, given/module-of
  save role-name, role-of(file)
  save role-part, <>
  fork test, not(is-equal(role-name, <>))
    hold
      save role-part, <#{role-name}>
  save lean-part, <>
  fork test, lean-of(file)
    hold
      save lean-part, <#lean>
  save deck-part, <>
  sift deck-of(file)
    case some
      link deck
      fork test, not(is-equal(deck/name, <>))
        hold
          save deck-part, <@{deck/name}>
    case none
      save nothing, 0
  save module-name, module-of(file)
  back <{role-part}{lean-part}{deck-part}\>{module-name}>

# a file's own part of the key: where it is, written portably, and its text's fingerprint
task file-part
  take run, like separate-run
  take file, like text
  like text
  mark private

  save unit, get-or-default(run/by-file, file, run/source)
  back <{portable-write(run/portable, file)}@{separate-cache/content-hash(unit/text)}>

# the unit key: own content (with each module's role and lean, which change what it mills to) and whatever else
# shapes the answer
task own-key
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like list, like text
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  save switch-key, given/switch-key
  save out, make list
  push(out, <separate>)
  fork test, state/uses-templates
    hold
      push(out, run/template-set/template-key)
    miss
      push(out, <>)
  push(out, given/env)
  fork test, is-equal(checked-as, state/as-import)
    hold
      push(out, <>)
    miss
      push(out, <entry:{portable-write(run/portable, checked-as)}>)
  push(out, switch-key())
  fork test, get(run/under-proof, state/at)
    hold
      push(out, <bodies>)
    miss
      push(out, <>)
  walk state/files
    take file
    save mine, file-part(run, file)
    push(out, <{mine}{read-part(run, file)}>)
  back out

# the run's key, for the memo: the whole surface of everything reached
task key-as
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like text
  mark private

  save fields, own-key(run, state, checked-as)
  walk state/dep-hashes
    take one
    push(fields, one)
  back separate-cache/hash-fields(fields)

# a unit's stub definitions, as the stored answer has them or worked out from its stubs
task defs-of
  take run, like separate-run
  take build, like unit-build
  like list, like name-def
  mark private

  sift build/defs
    case some
      link known
      back known
    case none
      save nothing, 0
  save surface, make list
  walk build/stubs
    take group
    walk group/statements
      take one
      push(surface, one)
  back name-defs(surface, run/tasks/outward)

# the build's name index grown to hold every unit before `up-to`
task index-names
  take run, like separate-run
  take up-to, like number
  like boolean
  mark private

  walk test
    hook test, is-below(run/unit-defs/length, up-to)
    hook hold
      save unit, run/unit-defs/length
      save defs, defs-of(run, get(run/builds, unit))
      push(run/unit-defs, defs)
      save place, 0
      walk defs
        take def
        walk def/gives
          take name
          save places, get-or-default(run/name-index, name, make list)
          save placed
            make def-at
              bind unit, unit
              bind at, place
          push(places, placed)
          save run/name-index/{name}, places
        save place, add(place, 1)
  back true

# the names the unit's own modules write, and the names their loads find. A module that does not mill uses nothing
task names-of-unit
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  like list, like text
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  save milled, given/milled
  save seen, make hash
  save out, make list
  walk state/files
    take file
    save unit, get-or-default(run/by-file, file, run/source)
    save one-milled, milled(unit, run/template-set/templates, run/template-set/template-key)
    fork test, one-milled/ok
      hold
        # read, never written: the mill cache holds this answer
        save milled-program, make list
        walk one-milled/program
          take one
          push(milled-program, one)
        walk names-used(milled-program)
          take name
          fork test, not(seen/has(name))
            hold
              save seen/{name}, true
              push(out, name)
    fork test, run/collected/scope/has(file)
      hold
        save scope-here, run/collected/scope/get(file)
        save find-names, scope-here/finds/keys()
        walk find-names
          take name
          fork test, not(seen/has(name))
            hold
              save seen/{name}, true
              push(out, name)
  back out

task used-of
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  like list, like text
  mark private

  sift state/used
    case some
      link known
      back known
    case none
      save nothing, 0
  save made, names-of-unit(run, state)
  save state/used, make(some, made)
  back made

# a unit's reach in dependency order
task reach-sorted
  take run, like separate-run
  take unit-at, like number
  like list, like number
  mark private

  save reached, get(run/reach, unit-at)
  back sort(reached/keys(), from-numbers)

# THE CACHE'S KEY, BY NAME (compile/names.tree): the fingerprints of only the dependency definitions this unit can reach
# by name, from the names its own modules write, read off the build's index
task named-key-as
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like text
  mark private

  save used, used-of(run, state)
  index-names(run, state/at)
  save sees, make hash
  walk reach-sorted(run, state/at)
    take d
    save sees/{d}, true
  save fields, make list
  push(fields, <names>)
  walk own-key(run, state, checked-as)
    take one
    push(fields, one)
  walk names-reached-indexed(run/name-index, run/unit-defs, sees, used, 1000000)
    take one
    push(fields, one)
  back separate-cache/hash-fields(fields)

# the name key, through a pointer kept under the whole-surface key: the same surface always gives the same name key,
# so a warm build reads the pointer and works out no names
task named-key-of
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  take surface-key, like text
  like text
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  fork test, given/has-cache
    hold
      save cached-name-key, given/cached-name-key
      back cached-name-key(<surface:{surface-key}>, job-of(run, state, checked-as))
  back named-key-as(run, state, checked-as)

# the inputs and their definitions for `term make --explain`
task reached-defs
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  like list, like name-def
  mark private

  sift state/defs
    case some
      link known
      back known
    case none
      save nothing, 0
  save out, make list
  walk reach-sorted(run, state/at)
    take d
    walk defs-of(run, get(run/builds, d))
      take def
      push(out, def)
  save state/defs, make(some, out)
  back out

# what the unit is built from, as `term make --explain` compares it: the same inputs its key is made of, each kept
# apart so a change can be named
task inputs-as
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like unit-inputs
  mark private

  save used, used-of(run, state)
  save defs, reached-defs(run, state)
  save key, own-key(run, state, checked-as)
  save given, run/given
  save unit-version, given/unit-version
  save compiler, unit-version()
  save own, make hash
  walk state/files
    take file
    save unit, get-or-default(run/by-file, file, run/source)
    save own/{file}, separate-cache/content-hash(unit/text)
  save read, make hash
  walk state/files
    take file
    save read/{file}, read-part(run, file)
  save settings, make list
  save k, 0
  walk test
    hook test, is-below(k, settings-count())
    hook hold
      push(settings, get(key, k))
      save k, add(k, 1)
  back
    make unit-inputs
      bind compiler, compiler
      bind own, own
      bind read, read
      bind settings, separate-cache/hash-fields(settings)
      bind names, names-printed(defs, used)

# ---- one unit built ----

# THE UNIT BUILT, checked as `checked-as`
task make-unit
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like unit-answer
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  save milled, given/milled
  save compile-unit, given/compile-unit

  # the stubs of every reachable unit, dependency order preserved, copied
  save program, make list
  walk reach-sorted(run, state/at)
    take d
    walk get(run/builds, d)/stubs
      take group
      walk copy-statements(group/statements)
        take one
        push(program, filed-in(one, group/file))

  save own-statements, make list
  save twins, make list
  walk state/files
    take file
    save unit, get-or-default(run/by-file, file, run/source)
    save one-milled, milled(unit, run/template-set/templates, run/template-set/template-key)
    fork test, not(one-milled/ok)
      hold
        # read, never written: the mill cache holds this answer
        save mill-errors, make list
        walk one-milled/diagnostics
          take mill-error
          push(mill-errors, mill-error)
        back refused-unit(mill-errors)
    walk one-milled/program
      take one
      save filed, filed-in(one, unit/file)
      push(program, filed)
      push(own-statements, filed)
    walk one-milled/twins
      take one-twin
      save one-twin/span/file, make(some, unit/file)
      push(twins, one-twin)

  # ONE NAMING PER UNIT, whichever entry reached it: the unit's own (first) file keeps its names, as the merged build
  # keeps the entry's
  save naming, get(state/files, 0)
  save result, compile-unit(program, checked-as, scope-of(run, state/at), naming, state/files)
  fork test, not(result/ok)
    hold
      back refused-unit(result/diagnostics)

  fork test, and(given/keep-program, is-equal(checked-as, run/source/file))
    hold
      save run/entry-program, make(some, result/program)

  # a twin is checked against the program it twins a task of, as the merged build checks it
  fork test, is-above(twins/length, 0)
    hold
      save twin-refused, as-diagnostics(separate-twin/check-twins(program, twins, checked-as))
      fork test, is-above(twin-refused/length, 0)
        hold
          back refused-unit(twin-refused)

  # this unit's emits: only its own files
  save own, make hash
  walk state/files
    take file
    save own/{file}, true
  save files-out, make list
  walk result/modules
    take emitted
    fork test, own/has(emitted/file)
      hold
        push(files-out, emitted)

  # the stub surface dependents check against, per own file, each task carrying what the whole-program analyses found
  # about it here, where its body is
  save known, as-known(separate-stub/stub-known(program))
  save stubbed, make list
  save surface, make list
  save under, get(run/under-proof, state/at)
  walk state/files
    take file
    save mine, make list
    walk own-statements
      take one
      fork test, is-equal(statement-file(one), file)
        hold
          push(mine, one)
    save stubs, stub-program(mine, make(some, known), under)
    save file-stubs
      make unit-stubs
        bind file, file
        bind statements, stubs
    push(stubbed, file-stubs)
    walk stubs
      take one
      push(surface, one)

  save own-docks, make list
  walk result/program
    take one
    sift one
      case dock
        fork test, own/has(statement-file(one))
          hold
            push(own-docks, one)
      miss
        turn next

  save entered, not(is-equal(checked-as, state/as-import))
  save open-claims, make none
  fork test, and(entered, is-above(result/open-claims/length, 0))
    hold
      save open-claims, make(some, result/open-claims)
  save obligations, make none
  fork test, entered
    hold
      save obligations, result/obligations

  save interface-hash, surface-hash(surface, run/tasks/outward)
  save surface-defs, name-defs(surface, run/tasks/outward)
  save routed, exported-route-calls(own-docks, result/program, own, given)
  save made
    make unit-build
      bind files, files-out
      bind stubs, stubbed
      bind interface-hash, interface-hash
      bind defs, make(some, surface-defs)
      bind docks, make(some, routed)
      bind roll, result/roll
      bind warnings, result/warnings
      bind open-claims, open-claims
      bind obligations, obligations
  back
    make unit-answer
      bind refused, make none
      bind build, make(some, made)

# WHAT A UNIT IS CHECKED WITH IS ITS OWN, and what it reaches: the walk's import scope cut to those files, so an importer
# never decides the unit's answer
task scope-of
  take run, like separate-run
  take unit-at, like number
  like hash, like text, like separate-scope
  mark private

  save sees, make hash
  walk get(run/order, unit-at)
    take file
    save sees/{file}, true
  walk reach-sorted(run, unit-at)
    take d
    walk get(run/order, d)
      take file
      save sees/{file}, true
  save out, make hash
  save scoped-files, run/collected/scope/keys()
  walk scoped-files
    take file
    fork test, sees/has(file)
      hold
        save out/{file}, run/collected/scope/get(file)
  back out

# the unit built this run, told why when the build explains
task built-now
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like unit-answer
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  save state/ran, true
  fork test, given/has-explain
    hold
      save now, inputs-as(run, state, checked-as)
      save recall, given/recall
      save reasons, make list
      sift recall(checked-as)
        case some
          link before
          save reasons, why(before, now)
        case none
          push(reasons, <nothing recorded: its first build, or the record was washed>)
      fork test, is-equal(reasons/length, 0)
        hold
          push(reasons, <its stored answer was missing>)
      save give-reasons, given/give-reasons
      give-reasons(state/label, reasons)
      save remember, given/remember
      remember(checked-as, now)
  back make-unit(run, state, checked-as)

# A STORED ANSWER, read back with this machine's roots. One that does not read back as a unit's answer is built again
task from-store
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take stored, like text
  like unit-answer
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  save restore, given/restore
  sift restore(portable-read(run/portable, stored))
    case some
      link value
      back value
    case none
      save state/ran, true
  back make-unit(run, state, state/answering)

# the unit checked as `checked-as`: this run's answer first, then the cache (memory, then disk), then a build
task answer-unit
  take run, like separate-run
  take state, like unit-state
  take checked-as, like text
  like unit-answer
  mark private

  save given, run/given
  save state/answering, checked-as
  save key, key-as(run, state, checked-as)
  save found, make none
  fork test, and(given/has-units, given/units/has(key))
    hold
      save memo-held, given/units/get(key)
      save found, make(some, memo-held)
  save answer, refused-unit(make list)
  sift found
    case some
      link memo
      save answer, memo
    case none
      fork test, given/has-cache
        hold
          save cached-unit, given/cached-unit
          save stored, cached-unit(named-key-of(run, state, checked-as, key), job-of(run, state, checked-as))
          save answer, from-store(run, state, stored)
        miss
          save answer, built-now(run, state, checked-as)
  fork test, given/has-units
    hold
      save given/units/{key}, answer
  back answer

# ---- the jobs the cache runs on a miss ----

# the unit built and stored, every deck's root a token, so the entry serves every clone
task job-stored
  take job, like unit-job
  like text

  save run, job/run
  save given, run/given
  save store, given/store
  save answer, built-now(run, job/state, job/checked-as)
  back portable-write(run/portable, store(answer))

# the unit's key by name
task job-named-key
  take job, like unit-job
  like text

  back named-key-as(job/run, job/state, job/checked-as)

# ---- the build ----

# whether a file states a top-level `rule`, read off its parse (the build's own memo)
task states-rule
  take given, like separate-given
  take unit, like token-source
  like boolean
  mark private

  save parsed, given/parsed
  save result, parsed(unit)
  fork test, not(result/ok)
    hold
      back false
  sift result/tree
    case root
      link nodes
      walk nodes
        take one
        sift one
          case group
            sift head-word(one)
              case some
                link word
                fork test, is-equal(word, <rule>)
                  hold
                    back true
              case none
                save nothing, 0
          miss
            turn next
  back false

# each unit's transitive dependency units, from the condensation: its direct ones in the order its files' edges name
# them, each with everything it reaches
task reach-of
  take order, like list, like list, like text
  take edges
    like hash
      like text
      like list, like text
  like list
    like hash
      like number
      like boolean
  mark private

  save unit-of, make hash
  save ui, 0
  walk order
    take group
    walk group
      take file
      save unit-of/{file}, ui
    save ui, add(ui, 1)
  save out, make list
  save ui, 0
  walk order
    take group
    save deps, make list
    save deps-seen, make hash
    walk group
      take file
      save targets, get-or-default(edges, file, make list)
      walk targets
        take dep
        save du, get-or-default(unit-of, dep, 0)
        fork test, and(not(is-equal(du, ui)), not(deps-seen/has(du)))
          hold
            save deps-seen/{du}, true
            push(deps, du)
    save reached, make hash
    walk deps
      take du
      save reached/{du}, true
      save further, get(out, du)
      save further-units, further/keys()
      walk further-units
        take t
        save reached/{t}, true
    push(out, reached)
    save ui, add(ui, 1)
  back out

# THE UNITS A PROOF REACHES (term-proof-0011): a unit proves when one of its files states a top-level `rule`, and every
# unit it reaches carries its bodies in its stubs, giving up the early cutoff for a body edit
task under-proof-of
  take given, like separate-given
  take by-file
    like hash
      like text
      like token-source
  take source, like token-source
  take order, like list, like list, like text
  take reach
    like list
      like hash
        like number
        like boolean
  like list, like boolean
  mark private

  save proven, make hash
  save uj, 0
  walk order
    take group
    save rule-stated, false
    walk group
      take file
      fork test, states-rule(given, get-or-default(by-file, file, source))
        hold
          save rule-stated, true
          halt
    fork test, rule-stated
      hold
        save reached, get(reach, uj)
        save reached-units, reached/keys()
        walk reached-units
          take d
          save proven/{d}, true
    save uj, add(uj, 1)
  save out, make list
  save uj, 0
  walk order
    take group
    push(out, proven/has(uj))
    save uj, add(uj, 1)
  back out

# THE SEPARATE BUILD of `source`'s closure
task compile-separate
  take source, like token-source
  take given, like separate-given
  like separate-answer

  save collect, given/collect
  save collected, collect()

  # a load the build cannot answer is refused with its own cause, as the merged build refuses it
  save load-errors, make list
  walk collected/diagnostics
    take found
    fork test, not(is-equal(found/severity, make warning))
      hold
        push(load-errors, found)
  fork test, is-above(load-errors/length, 0)
    hold
      back refused-answer(load-errors)

  save sources, collected/sources

  # THE SAME UNIT IS THE SAME ENTRY ON EVERY MACHINE: each deck's root is written as a token
  save deck-of, given/deck-of
  save decks, make list
  walk sources
    take unit
    sift deck-of(unit/file)
      case some
        link deck
        push(decks, deck)
      case none
        save nothing, 0
  save held-roots, portable-by(decks)
  save tasks-of, given/portable-tasks

  # the edges the walk itself followed, injected runtimes included
  save edges, collected/edges
  save files, make list
  walk sources
    take unit
    push(files, unit/file)
  save order, units(files, edges)
  save by-file, make hash
  walk sources
    take unit
    save by-file/{unit/file}, unit

  # templates are global, so gathered once, exactly as the merged build gathers them
  save parsed, given/parsed
  save template-set, graph-templates(sources, parsed)

  save reach, reach-of(order, edges)
  save proving, under-proof-of(given, by-file, source, order, reach)

  save run
    make separate-run
      bind source, source
      bind given, given
      bind portable, held-roots
      bind tasks, tasks-of(held-roots)
      bind collected, collected
      bind by-file, by-file
      bind order, order
      bind reach, reach
      bind under-proof, proving
      bind template-set, template-set
      bind builds, make list
      bind name-index, make hash
      bind unit-defs, make list
      bind entry-program, make none

  save built, make list
  save reused, make list
  save all-modules
    like hash
      like text
      like dynamic
    make hash
  save all-warnings, make list
  save open-claims, make none
  save obligations, make none
  # typed where it is made: its key is a text built in an arm, which inference has not met here
  save exports
    like hash
      like text
      like export-entry
    make hash
  save closure-keys, make list
  save natives, make list
  save docks, make list
  save rolls, make list
  save surface-program, make list
  save role-of, given/role-of

  save ui, 0
  walk order
    take group
    save label, join(group, <+>)

    # THE ENTRY'S OWN UNIT IS CHECKED AS THE ENTRY, and any other unit under a name no statement carries, so its
    # answer does not depend on which entry reached it. A ONE-FILE UNIT IS CHECKED AS ITSELF, whichever entry reached
    # it, and asked again as an import only when that fails
    save entry, false
    walk group
      take file
      fork test, is-equal(file, source/file)
        hold
          save entry, true
    save first-file, get(group, 0)
    save as-import, <{first-file}#unit>
    save as-self, make none
    save asked-first, as-import
    fork test, entry
      hold
        save as-self, make(some, source/file)
        save asked-first, source/file
      miss
        fork test, is-equal(group/length, 1)
          hold
            save as-self, make(some, first-file)
            save asked-first, first-file

    # every reachable dependency unit's fingerprint: a body-only edit leaves it, and so the key, where it was
    save dep-hashes, make list
    walk reach-sorted(run, ui)
      take d
      save dep-build, get(run/builds, d)
      push(dep-hashes, dep-build/interface-hash)
    save dep-hashes, sort(dep-hashes, from-texts)

    save uses-templates, false
    walk group
      take file
      save unit, get-or-default(by-file, file, source)
      fork test, or(is-equal(role-of(file), <view>), writes-fuse(unit/text))
        hold
          save uses-templates, true
          halt

    save state
      make unit-state
        bind at, ui
        bind files, group
        bind label, label
        bind entry, entry
        bind as-import, as-import
        bind as-self, as-self
        bind dep-hashes, dep-hashes
        bind uses-templates, uses-templates
        bind used, make none
        bind defs, make none
        bind ran, false
        bind answering, asked-first

    push(closure-keys, key-as(run, state, asked-first))

    save cached, answer-unit(run, state, asked-first)
    # a one-file unit that fails as itself may still build as an import: an import is held only to what the program as
    # a whole owes, as the merged build holds a module it reaches
    sift cached/refused
      case some
        link found
        fork test, and(not(entry), is-unequal(asked-first, as-import))
          hold
            save cached, answer-unit(run, state, as-import)
      case none
        save nothing, 0

    sift cached/refused
      case some
        link found
        back refused-answer(found)
      case none
        save nothing, 0

    sift cached/build
      case some
        link build
        fork test, state/ran
          hold
            push(built, label)
          miss
            push(reused, label)
        push(run/builds, build)
        walk build/files
          take emitted
          save all-modules/{emitted/file}, emitted/emit
        sift build/docks
          case some
            link own-docks
            walk own-docks
              take one
              push(docks, one)
          case none
            save nothing, 0
        sift build/roll
          case some
            link roll
            save rolled
              make unit-roll
                bind label, label
                bind roll, roll
            push(rolls, rolled)
          case none
            save nothing, 0
        walk build/warnings
          take warned
          push(all-warnings, warned)
        fork test, entry
          hold
            save open-claims, build/open-claims
            save obligations, build/obligations

        # the surface, in dependency order, so a later definition of a name replaces an earlier one
        walk build/stubs
          take group-stubs
          walk group-stubs/statements
            take one
            sift one
              case native
                push(natives, one)
              miss
                save nothing, 0
            fork test, given/keep-program
              hold
                push(surface-program, one)
            sift exported-of(one, group-stubs/file, given)
              case some
                link made
                save export-key, <value:{made/name}>
                fork test, made/type
                  hold
                    save export-key, <type:{made/name}>
                save exports/{export-key}, made
              case none
                save nothing, 0
      case none
        save nothing, 0
    save ui, add(ui, 1)

  # the entry's own spelling, warned about once, for the file the build was asked for
  walk entry-warnings(source, sources, parsed, template-set/templates)
    take warned
    push(all-warnings, warned)

  back
    make separate-answer
      bind refused, make none
      bind modules, all-modules
      bind warnings, all-warnings
      bind open-claims, open-claims
      bind obligations, obligations
      bind exports, exports/values()
      bind built, built
      bind reused, reused
      bind closure-key, separate-cache/hash-fields(closure-keys)
      bind natives, natives
      bind docks, docks
      bind rolls, rolls
      bind program, run/entry-program
      bind surface, surface-program

# what a stub definition exports: a public task or a constant as a value, a form or a mask as a type. A private task is
# in the stub for the privacy checks, and is no part of what an entry's shim exports
task exported-of
  take one, like statement
  take file, like text
  take given, like separate-given
  like maybe, like export-entry
  mark private

  save has-export, given/has-stub-export
  sift one
    case function
      link name
      link stub-export
      fork test, one/private
        hold
          back make none
      save made, export-made(name, stub-export, has-export(one), file, false)
      back make(some, made)
    case let
      link name
      link stub-export
      save made, export-made(name, stub-export, has-export(one), file, false)
      back make(some, made)
    case record-type
      link name
      link stub-export
      save made, export-made(name, stub-export, has-export(one), file, true)
      back make(some, made)
    case mask
      link name
      link stub-export
      save made, export-made(name, stub-export, has-export(one), file, true)
      back make(some, made)
    miss
      back make none
  back make none

task export-made
  take name, like text
  take stub-export, like text
  take export-given, like boolean
  take file, like text
  take is-type, like boolean
  like export-entry
  mark private

  save exported, name
  fork test, export-given
    hold
      save exported, stub-export
  back
    make export-entry
      bind name, name
      bind exported, exported
      bind file, file
      bind type, is-type
